<!--Post: 895--><!--Time: 1093413518-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST895"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, August 24, 2004 - 10:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->From profiler Pat Brown&#39;s website:  <BR>&#34;PJ’s may refer to a business like PJ’s Restaurant and Pub, etc&#34;  <BR> <BR>&#34;BTK most likely speaks Spanish fluently&#34;  <BR> <BR>&#34;the PJ’s Chapter is listed under the chapter labeled BTK’s Haunts &#40;maybe meaning places he liked to hang out&#41;&#34;  <BR> <BR>--------------------------------  <BR> <BR>Ok, a few days ago I received an e-mail at catchBTK.com from someone who claimed there was a mall-type restaurant/pub/diner &#40;I can&#39;t remember which&#41; in Wichita called &#34;PJ&#39;s&#34; that opened in the mid 1970s and that a lot of Hispanics worked there and perhaps it was what BTK was referring to with his &#34;PJ&#39;s&#34; reference.  <BR> <BR>Unfortunately, his e-mail was lost &#40;along with some other data&#41; and I can&#39;t follow up. Help? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 895-->
<!--Post: 897--><!--Time: 1093439172-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST897"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, August 25, 2004 - 6:06 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I do agree with the concept that &#39;Haunts&#39; refers to places that BTK likes to frequent. He may &#39;tour&#39; some of his killing sites, but despite the fact that he has avoided capture, he has patterns. You can bet that he trolls like all serial killers. <BR> <BR>It is interesting about BTK speaking Spanish. If his appearance lends itself to something other than WASP, that would greatly assist him in alluding the police. I do think that wearing a skull cap during his assaults indicates that he is trying to hide some distinct feature in his appearance. Why cover one&#39;s hair and leave the face exposed? There is always method in one&#39;s madness.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 897-->
<!--Post: 898--><!--Time: 1093445317-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST898"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, August 25, 2004 - 7:48 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->On a simple search for other PJ refernces in Witchita: <BR> <BR>A person: <a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/contact_us/contact_list/newspaper_staff_np1/6302728.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/contact_us/contac t_list/newspaper_staff_np1/6302728.htm</a> <BR> <BR>A business site: <a href="http://www.nationjob.com/pjcompany/ifrs" target=_top>http://www.nationjob.com/pjcompany/ifrs</a> <BR> <BR>There are some PJ colleges on the web.  One of which had a table outlining which classes at Witchita University would be worth credits. <BR> <BR>There is a PapaJohn&#39;s in Witchita and some sites have shortened it to PJ&#39;s <BR> <BR>There are many meanings for PJ in Witchita, and PJ Wyatt is only one of them.  Why the Police singaled her out specifically is strange, and I can only assume that they know something we don&#39;t.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 898-->
<!--Post: 915--><!--Time: 1093566185-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST915"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 26, 2004 - 5:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Teardrop,Did the hat cover enough of his head that no hair was seen? Maybe he has a shaved head , or a bald spot that would help someone ID him. Hair can change the way a man looks,just check out the hair club for men and see how different they look. Women can change thier hair doo but still look like them selves.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 915-->
<!--Post: 1043--><!--Time: 1095341718-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1043"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, September 16, 2004 - 6:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sandy: Kevin stated that he had the cap pulled so low over his face that he could hardly see the killer&#39;s eyes. I would have used a ski mask myself. Of course, BTK knew that he would not leave any living witnessses, or so he thought. I just find it very odd that he would cover his head and not his face.  <BR> <BR>Different events occur in lives. Maybe he was having chemo or had surgery, or an accident that temporarily affected his appearance by making him more easily identifiable. My mother had a brain tumor and surgery for it. It was quite obvious until her hair grew back.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1043-->
